    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-20T11:16:13+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T11:16:13+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T00:46:13Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T00:46:13Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system in the Bight will drift southeast as the associated trough crosses eastern South Australia clears before clearing later Friday. A weak high pressure system briefly moves across southern SA later Friday before a trough and cold front then move into the west from Saturday evening and cross the rest of SA on Sunday. A high will then push in behind the front and will move across the Bight early next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the middle of the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 32 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west in the late afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h in the morning then tending north to northwesterly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching around 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny day. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla in the evening. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending southerly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 19 and 28 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds south to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
